stion/id #uuid "51778192-f0d9-5b42-8f6c-c91972dca2dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-51346" :question/problem "If $h(x)=5-10x,$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=5-10x,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=5-10y\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5-10y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-10 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51346/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51346"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32630/selection/fba1a4a757f11e2ed6ef290c52a138d95212490dca7cbdc69a89d585552ef029" :answer/id #uuid "a9086fb1-0bf7-53b6-ad04-13901c28736a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32630/selection/44fef7068c700b96060415d209c9a0b895c85dfa582aae858d38b52fb614cde3" :answer/id #uuid "873e11a8-6198-5715-93ae-5a8f613630aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+5({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32630/selection/c8ae1c28ec42871f34a3127bf928208f55dc7242406aa648277f9e0f8f362682" :answer/id #uuid "67540016-27b6-5122-b2e6-aba830d94ae9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32630/selection/9d44ff3e4e4fb6e2b808b430220c03a9692d622da05e0865c2a0fbd9930016d5" :answer/id #uuid "91a4e266-f381-5573-8397-cd010528fb7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32630/selection/ff14c8fd1159ecc2f989d9fe12b6e89bc48808184d10ed1953dc75584e12d53d" :answer/id #uuid "a503fd42-eab2-5156-ad87-3df25a4f1826" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-{h}^{-1}(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32630/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93bdb2f7-562a-54f7-ad88-5cf15ec1316e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32630/selection/fba1a4a757f11e2ed6ef290c52a138d95212490dca7cbdc69a89d585552ef029" :answer-field/choices ["q-32630/selection/fba1a4a757f11e2ed6ef290c52a138d95212490dca7cbdc69a89d585552ef029" "q-32630/selection/44fef7068c700b96060415d209c9a0b895c85dfa582aae858d38b52fb614cde3" "q-32630/selection/c8ae1c28ec42871f34a3127bf928208f55dc7242406aa648277f9e0f8f362682" "q-32630/selection/9d44ff3e4e4fb6e2b808b430220c03a9692d622da05e0865c2a0fbd9930016d5" "q-32630/selection/ff14c8fd1159ecc2f989d9fe12b6e89bc48808184d10ed1953dc75584e12d53d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32630" :question/id #uuid "5c8e44eb-6281-567e-910f-a87e302bbb5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32630" :question/problem "If $h(x)=2{x}^{5}+3{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}+6,$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=2{x}^{5}+3{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}+6,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=2{y}^{5}+3{y}^{4}-{y}^{3}+6\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{5}+3{y}^{4}-{y}^{3}+6) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =10{y}^{4}+12{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{10{y}^{4}+12{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-32630/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32630"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47990/selection/6bc3aa0636349bfa10909ce8787b8a3ef824a4f2bd964e1c986de3565875bf2a" :answer/id #uuid "04008d50-f0f3-5018-ab41-fdf2bf3f4dad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{g}^{-1}(x)}{2{g}^{-1}(x)+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47990/selection/7d7ba7dd63d51eb9b131fbfa996e439857b2c632e2fc7da8b661fda4021453bc" :answer/id #uuid "bbbda5bc-73ea-54b5-b3cc-6dd77336d2d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{2}}{2{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{3}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47990/selection/acb6ee26bddbc348c03e81cf09786bceed71955ef40c69ff304085c38bce7a01" :answer/id #uuid "8ebbd05c-6df4-5194-b2db-6c3ef051943d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2{g}^{-1}(x)}{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47990/selection/f9f97306395e3c5f425241d0f340c40f390d559ea347ac09b62493b692eefe2d" :answer/id #uuid "d549f174-016a-51b6-a4a3-ee20ebe4ddee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{2}}{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{3}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47990/selection/87a37a4b3e3e683de5eac1ea4c2e273c3717e9ce97661e9608a6655671ed80cf" :answer/id #uuid "5f4b53b2-a308-5a96-b324-b720bd818d8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{g}^{-1}(x)}{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{3}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47990/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "19b5919a-3cd7-5a00-8986-783114b246da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47990/selection/7d7ba7dd63d51eb9b131fbfa996e439857b2c632e2fc7da8b661fda4021453bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-47990/selection/6bc3aa0636349bfa10909ce8787b8a3ef824a4f2bd964e1c986de3565875bf2a" "q-47990/selection/7d7ba7dd63d51eb9b131fbfa996e439857b2c632e2fc7da8b661fda4021453bc" "q-47990/selection/acb6ee26bddbc348c03e81cf09786bceed71955ef40c69ff304085c38bce7a01" "q-47990/selection/f9f97306395e3c5f425241d0f340c40f390d559ea347ac09b62493b692eefe2d" "q-47990/selection/87a37a4b3e3e683de5eac1ea4c2e273c3717e9ce97661e9608a6655671ed80cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47990" :question/id #uuid "e6754b71-0370-53e2-a5c7-4082cebe7afd" :question/math-academy-id "q-47990" :question/problem "If $g(x)=-{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{x},$ find ${({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${g}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=-{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{x},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=-{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{y}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{y}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-2y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-\\frac{2{y}^{3}+2}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{3}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =-\\frac{({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}}{2({g}^{-1}(x))^{3}+2} \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}}{2({g}^{-1}(x))^{3}+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47990/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47990"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3301/selection/0d0e1a2a80170a871f6ff009c50a464bbfe0768a537043ec8ef884c5be078c3b" :answer/id #uuid "52e47992-be85-5808-bea1-5863be7f62e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12{f}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3301/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" :answer/id #uuid "7d3e45b6-cbca-5663-8471-e9c9dc66ce66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3301/selection/cf10a81a167821ddf82ca1d5c29d8c68918b74194caa20d6c4079a305fc4d0b5" :answer/id #uuid "e8697f18-e1a0-5f4c-b694-eef13cb7cd65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{f}^{-1}(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3301/selection/5b7709daae154a43623a115b407f64fd58897348cce9f3d5d5282a233a713504" :answer/id #uuid "31e8165b-164b-5146-abd0-514876d77fac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3301/selection/102dce14a3cbc66fc8f10c60e52ed2eac8351ed9d3a6bb9c9f8a475e47600390" :answer/id #uuid "d8b0f6d7-a852-5c2e-a141-c8b2d64b1df2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{12{f}^{-1}(x)+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3301/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "faf927c1-0ab6-5b22-84a5-cbf0869ad473" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3301/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" :answer-field/choices ["q-3301/selection/0d0e1a2a80170a871f6ff009c50a464bbfe0768a537043ec8ef884c5be078c3b" "q-3301/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" "q-3301/selection/cf10a81a167821ddf82ca1d5c29d8c68918b74194caa20d6c4079a305fc4d0b5" "q-3301/selection/5b7709daae154a43623a115b407f64fd58897348cce9f3d5d5282a233a713504" "q-3301/selection/102dce14a3cbc66fc8f10c60e52ed2eac8351ed9d3a6bb9c9f8a475e47600390"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3301" :question/id #uuid "533c7ada-5c96-5084-9f1e-d356ac9d1079" :question/math-academy-id "q-3301" :question/problem "If $f(x)=12x+5,$ find ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${f}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=12x+5,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=12y+5\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(12y+5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{12} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3301/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3301"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3298/selection/b1f765f3596b456a5f390ad623789d37ea7ac1d0f528aee947710676b83ef037" :answer/id #uuid "f1943f48-f68d-5be9-8971-aa2306163e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}+{g}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3298/selection/260e792e30c4015d7689151ecbb9198e1d1b3b18644c079f91bd5b2caf57238b" :answer/id #uuid "132846aa-91ad-51b7-88fe-305b23e93eab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3298/selection/d190c643f1e3431c3f968a1b000d996ee12ef8c4ff9e9ccbe5a4de0782ca4136" :answer/id #uuid "ca1f1132-d4e2-56d4-8eb2-866861de658e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3298/selection/cc8eddfdb99c9764eecd0468498ed05cde7a4f1d9ddc27789774c6baeff548ba" :answer/id #uuid "6b961df8-8962-5662-b60c-1c56f9475cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3298/selection/ab7cc532a5fe14f638f914b517e0f6fc1008fc0b8f98a95f9e3dc6c6c6806b9d" :answer/id #uuid "4515f787-3974-51b1-bdb7-1a620170002c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}+{g}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3298/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52ad1901-9912-5ea2-bdb9-7a78de5bee9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3298/selection/d190c643f1e3431c3f968a1b000d996ee12ef8c4ff9e9ccbe5a4de0782ca4136" :answer-field/choices ["q-3298/selection/b1f765f3596b456a5f390ad623789d37ea7ac1d0f528aee947710676b83ef037" "q-3298/selection/260e792e30c4015d7689151ecbb9198e1d1b3b18644c079f91bd5b2caf57238b" "q-3298/selection/d190c643f1e3431c3f968a1b000d996ee12ef8c4ff9e9ccbe5a4de0782ca4136" "q-3298/selection/cc8eddfdb99c9764eecd0468498ed05cde7a4f1d9ddc27789774c6baeff548ba" "q-3298/selection/ab7cc532a5fe14f638f914b517e0f6fc1008fc0b8f98a95f9e3dc6c6c6806b9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3298" :question/id #uuid "8595e807-03d0-5bb1-b8e2-2356f1d62071" :question/math-academy-id "q-3298" :question/problem "Find ${({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$  as a function of ${g}^{-1}(x),$ if $g(x)=8{x}^{2}+x.$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=8{x}^{2}+x,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=8{y}^{2}+y\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(8{y}^{2}+y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =16y+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{16y+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)+1} \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3298/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3298"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32646/selection/4e5ee79ee1726a7e588b5a9ae56168eea1b11267e2583827d10b254b07f01ae1" :answer/id #uuid "987e8fc5-29f7-56ef-9590-c66bffb514ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{{h}^{-1}(x)}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32646/selection/c11d40dedfe4c99594369dc7e5fafa909933d2c5012695d7ae074b3ef4a3759b" :answer/id #uuid "828fadad-dc69-5606-96ef-7ef202f10561" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32646/selection/45cd584b7d956af105124c97397ef2127dc3e544a64e19aace533d2aaaa2d507" :answer/id #uuid "cb1e9d53-179b-5633-b94d-88a276d3ccb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32646/selection/348bcc130c81e97b1f9d96ccb958fb6cb86a512ce4262676c7679aaec73c845f" :answer/id #uuid "84ddc5ec-746d-57f9-8684-1f7283aaa0f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32646/selection/3ac86d97c37b3ea3073135c028942d79d34bc2fbf77bb69340c10a551aabbf88" :answer/id #uuid "0c68605c-ef3b-5157-a9c8-12772337e22c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{{h}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32646/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf8bde2-020d-56ac-8cec-37f51ff5b83e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32646/selection/348bcc130c81e97b1f9d96ccb958fb6cb86a512ce4262676c7679aaec73c845f" :answer-field/choices ["q-32646/selection/4e5ee79ee1726a7e588b5a9ae56168eea1b11267e2583827d10b254b07f01ae1" "q-32646/selection/c11d40dedfe4c99594369dc7e5fafa909933d2c5012695d7ae074b3ef4a3759b" "q-32646/selection/45cd584b7d956af105124c97397ef2127dc3e544a64e19aace533d2aaaa2d507" "q-32646/selection/348bcc130c81e97b1f9d96ccb958fb6cb86a512ce4262676c7679aaec73c845f" "q-32646/selection/3ac86d97c37b3ea3073135c028942d79d34bc2fbf77bb69340c10a551aabbf88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32646" :question/id #uuid "4e8c657c-bed2-5e72-8393-f6026f0c3dfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-32646" :question/problem "If $h(x)={2}^{x+1},$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y={2}^{x+1},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx={2}^{y+1}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({2}^{y+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & ={2}^{y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{2}^{-y}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-32646/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0196af83-9ef6-5bab-9f50-0aacf488f0cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32646"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51347/selection/6bcf0c709c697591259b6fca029a166447a177b69185d348d384bdb70092daf9" :answer/id #uuid "8a42b882-8d02-5557-9935-d77ff2672e9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51347/selection/59564af060b3b40aa22692b13c0a5607c983110521f45380fd5d6e52f73442ee" :answer/id #uuid "1f38e994-012f-58f1-9102-4dde98374e4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51347/selection/959f7c5de4e4415530bef18526b41f068f14de0f81e39775e5f4b7a1bb6c5b9f" :answer/id #uuid "99c1aabf-e9f4-5db0-90a2-d7c0892a2c82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51347/selection/5affb0bf29873ea5ad81bd6efa67e26e6b5d7f9c4b2ad72d8a1dc82bcac6a0ca" :answer/id #uuid "05f95817-4676-570d-a02e-818cb8b8c25e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51347/selection/f1f2306d5375a7ac5606611526b424d9fa2a86945968e8ec53619d7c0c0d8178" :answer/id #uuid "1f38ba86-b8e9-5d71-ac9f-e2b319e4dc39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51347/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa489ab8-7e07-5c73-a0f5-1c9ba5ad3cef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51347/selection/f1f2306d5375a7ac5606611526b424d9fa2a86945968e8ec53619d7c0c0d8178" :answer-field/choices ["q-51347/selection/6bcf0c709c697591259b6fca029a166447a177b69185d348d384bdb70092daf9" "q-51347/selection/59564af060b3b40aa22692b13c0a5607c983110521f45380fd5d6e52f73442ee" "q-51347/selection/959f7c5de4e4415530bef18526b41f068f14de0f81e39775e5f4b7a1bb6c5b9f" "q-51347/selection/5affb0bf29873ea5ad81bd6efa67e26e6b5d7f9c4b2ad72d8a1dc82bcac6a0ca" "q-51347/selection/f1f2306d5375a7ac5606611526b424d9fa2a86945968e8ec53619d7c0c0d8178"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51347" :question/id #uuid "48971e60-851c-5e83-9769-837fe072fbcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-51347" :question/problem "If $h(x)=\\sqrt{2x+5},$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\sqrt{2x+5},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2y+5}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{2y+5}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}((2y+5)^{1/2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{1}{2}(2y+5)^{-1/2}\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2y+5}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{2y+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-51347/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0196af83-9ef6-5bab-9f50-0aacf488f0cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32643/selection/6dca9be185173a948517b2d6da82d236d91dfdf222f631e8e7360e5239625cff" :answer/id #uuid "e65b2cd2-e670-5799-b5e8-0458c719d5b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})}{6{f}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32643/selection/9a5cb22232b2bf4fb88ac2f45945d8864b606e404f4c1abfcc2cb796251fc938" :answer/id #uuid "0ed2f9fc-17b0-5803-9a34-50d1f606b8d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})}{6{f}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32643/selection/d721e716d33aada2534dbeae69c00b2dcb29a302f0b840d6c82f9135f404df47" :answer/id #uuid "3790ddb8-be3b-586f-9027-107072b3fc45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})}{6{f}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32643/selection/85e4e0147fb15e81a60b3e04c43f440820e88b21c8b514711e81e10ed40a2399" :answer/id #uuid "bf31c046-eaea-569a-a500-3925e906dcc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})}{6{f}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32643/selection/b0e80884170425a1267d22ef71a7bd91e58603b0cb2454c3b6ce8cdeac9949bd" :answer/id #uuid "7ea5d838-2e58-5800-b966-df057f630492" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})}{{f}^{-1}(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32643/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b072317-c200-5ab3-b218-6871ce3ddb9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32643/selection/6dca9be185173a948517b2d6da82d236d91dfdf222f631e8e7360e5239625cff" :answer-field/choices ["q-32643/selection/6dca9be185173a948517b2d6da82d236d91dfdf222f631e8e7360e5239625cff" "q-32643/selection/9a5cb22232b2bf4fb88ac2f45945d8864b606e404f4c1abfcc2cb796251fc938" "q-32643/selection/d721e716d33aada2534dbeae69c00b2dcb29a302f0b840d6c82f9135f404df47" "q-32643/selection/85e4e0147fb15e81a60b3e04c43f440820e88b21c8b514711e81e10ed40a2399" "q-32643/selection/b0e80884170425a1267d22ef71a7bd91e58603b0cb2454c3b6ce8cdeac9949bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32643" :question/id #uuid "080cbed3-e50e-5a9a-9cd4-f26407b6f966" :question/math-academy-id "q-32643" :question/problem "If $f(x)={sin}^{3}⁡({x}^{2}),$ find ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${f}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y={sin}^{3}⁡({x}^{2}),$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx={sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{2})\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =3{sin}^{2}⁡({y}^{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\cdot 2y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =6y{sin}^{2}⁡({y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{6y{sin}^{2}⁡({y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡({y}^{2})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({y}^{2})}{6y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})}{6{f}^{-1}(x)} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2})}{6{f}^{-1}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-32643/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0196af83-9ef6-5bab-9f50-0aacf488f0cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32635/selection/16cb19438caa07a5128fb5239613846e05b1135ab7929cdfd13eab72bc5b8009" :answer/id #uuid "bae88753-fe0c-5730-90e0-24a7367a988f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32635/selection/12fc667829c225dc4ec137901b08a5a70d3be8c74437e5c928b5504059e7a470" :answer/id #uuid "3410f762-ea3c-5fae-90f5-092500ff7908" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32635/selection/9108312ce3103f3dc743263b8d33e02d8ca32ce611d033485d55ee637f202b87" :answer/id #uuid "70ef8451-980a-5993-a2df-8a29791868dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32635/selection/716ab2f3cfbc05863001894c6dd0e858ec47296690267adc56da3e5e97d0ca09" :answer/id #uuid "e691b867-b706-5476-a668-64e67f9f26c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32635/selection/ff81d111f5aba7504913a0bf1bb7c3049d8136fd5dbec0bd6772571259c2ac55" :answer/id #uuid "b7ade4f6-6f45-5c32-a6de-d34a0dc6fd48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32635/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60906cdb-5041-50be-ae27-7859b2067606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32635/selection/12fc667829c225dc4ec137901b08a5a70d3be8c74437e5c928b5504059e7a470" :answer-field/choices ["q-32635/selection/16cb19438caa07a5128fb5239613846e05b1135ab7929cdfd13eab72bc5b8009" "q-32635/selection/12fc667829c225dc4ec137901b08a5a70d3be8c74437e5c928b5504059e7a470" "q-32635/selection/9108312ce3103f3dc743263b8d33e02d8ca32ce611d033485d55ee637f202b87" "q-32635/selection/716ab2f3cfbc05863001894c6dd0e858ec47296690267adc56da3e5e97d0ca09" "q-32635/selection/ff81d111f5aba7504913a0bf1bb7c3049d8136fd5dbec0bd6772571259c2ac55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32635" :question/id #uuid "562e91c5-a627-5456-91fe-61cfb99ce273" :question/math-academy-id "q-32635" :question/problem "If $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+5)-1,$ find ${({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${g}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+5)-1,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+5)-1\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+5)-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5)\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2y+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5) \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32635/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0196af83-9ef6-5bab-9f50-0aacf488f0cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73074/selection/d36537424c9499b520e3934c25d6059d10abca3c1109ae70d53e01b64cc65650" :answer/id #uuid "74db09bd-e041-5da6-94e0-5c7083e23640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{p}^{-1}(x)+2)-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({p}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73074/selection/e1ae732bf43ecd96aa8014feb929b97903d8c5bf3ccf40171eda38610a271ef7" :answer/id #uuid "3d94c654-8062-5e6e-8e01-0b53ad8cf631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡({p}^{-1}(x))-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{p}^{-1}(x)+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73074/selection/7feb3cd040383c0214fb780eeb20f4307d41523da773fd0d21a5b45c3c2259e7" :answer/id #uuid "7fb0a434-ca40-5460-8833-f8480d9ba5ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡({p}^{-1}(x))-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{p}^{-1}(x)+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73074/selection/b5bfc0c12202a31651b392d2084ed0ba76518ab4adfb081b56a68c7dc3fbbf87" :answer/id #uuid "d759675c-fcb9-5210-a758-0ac90b38af91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡({p}^{-1}(x))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{p}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73074/selection/e2e40ec4dbd2b544cd879963fd7b62f0f9a219299eef14c7fa800cd00f5cdbe2" :answer/id #uuid "149dfa98-479a-5454-8376-d096eb6968da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡({p}^{-1}(x))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73074/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54db1bf1-5e61-5f57-93f4-eebac33a7fdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73074/selection/7feb3cd040383c0214fb780eeb20f4307d41523da773fd0d21a5b45c3c2259e7" :answer-field/choices ["q-73074/selection/d36537424c9499b520e3934c25d6059d10abca3c1109ae70d53e01b64cc65650" "q-73074/selection/e1ae732bf43ecd96aa8014feb929b97903d8c5bf3ccf40171eda38610a271ef7" "q-73074/selection/7feb3cd040383c0214fb780eeb20f4307d41523da773fd0d21a5b45c3c2259e7" "q-73074/selection/b5bfc0c12202a31651b392d2084ed0ba76518ab4adfb081b56a68c7dc3fbbf87" "q-73074/selection/e2e40ec4dbd2b544cd879963fd7b62f0f9a219299eef14c7fa800cd00f5cdbe2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73074" :question/id #uuid "5546ec10-c37f-5467-9245-0277167930fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-73074" :question/problem "If $p(x)=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x+1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ find ${({p}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${p}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x+1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2y+1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={p}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal. Notice that we will use of the trigonometric identity $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2y+1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+1)\\cdot 2+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4y+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4y+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${p}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={p}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{p}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡({p}^{-1}(x))-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{p}^{-1}(x)+2)} \\\\ {({p}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡({p}^{-1}(x))-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{p}^{-1}(x)+2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73074/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0196af83-9ef6-5bab-9f50-0aacf488f0cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73074"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-196"] :question/problem "If $f(x)=3x^2+9,$ find $(f^{-1})'(x)$ as a function of $f^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y = 3x^2+9,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=3y^2+9\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y=f^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\dfrac{ \\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3{y}^{2}+9) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =6y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{6y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of $f^{-1}(x).$ Since $y=f^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{6{f}^{-1}(x)} \\\\ ({f}^{-1})^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{6{f}^{-1}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-197"] :question/problem "Find $\\left(f^{-1}\\right)'(x)$ as a function of $f^{-1}(x)$ if $f(x) = \\cos \\left(x^2\\right) +6.$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y = \\cos \\left(x^2\\right) +6,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\cos \\left(y^2\\right) + 6\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y=f^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\dfrac{ \\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})+6] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2y}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of $f^{-1}(x).$ Since $y=f^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =-\\frac{1}{2({f}^{-1}(x))}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}) \\\\ ({f}^{-1})^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{2({f}^{-1}(x))}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
